    "body": "## Security impact\n\nPrivate chat access still loaded a job globally by numeric `jobId` before checking whether the caller was the owner or assigned worker. An authenticated outsider therefore received `403` for an existing private conversation but `404` for a nonexistent job, creating an existence oracle over private job/chat activity. The same access policy is used by REST chat history/send paths and WebSocket chat-topic authorization.\n\n## Fix\n\n- resolve chat access through the existing participant-scoped `JobRepository.findParticipantById(jobId, userId)` query;\n- return the existing neutral job-not-found response for both missing jobs and non-participants;\n- fail closed before repository access when the authenticated principal has no persisted user id;\n- preserve existing lifecycle rules: completed chats remain readable, inactive chats remain read-only, and active accepted chats remain sendable.\n\n## Tests\n\n- outsider access now exercises only the participant-scoped lookup and receives neutral not-found;\n- missing authenticated identity fails closed without any repository query;\n- owner read-only behavior after completion remains covered;\n- worker send behavior for active accepted jobs remains covered;\n- runtime container smoke now asserts `404` for outsider chat history, replacing the stale pre-hardening `403` contract.\n\n## CI note\n\nThe first head passed Maven verify, web verify, compose contract and Container Security. Runtime smoke failed exactly at its stale outsider-chat `403` assertion after the production behavior correctly changed to `404`; the smoke assertion was updated in the new head. No production authorization rule was relaxed.\n\n## Merge gate\n\nMerge only after all checks on the new exact head are green, `master` is revalidated and has not moved (or the branch is safely rebased), then merge with a merge commit using the exact checked head SHA. Verify post-merge master workflows before starting another slice.",
